0..69 Comment "// The obligation `include` creates: the included theory\'s rules join"
70..147 Comment "// the including block\'s, and the union is completed as one block. Each block"
148..223 Comment "// below completes alone; the union leaves a critical pair whose two normal"
224..294 Comment "// forms are one call with its arguments swapped, which the path order"
295..361 Comment "// orients neither way, so the including block is refused by name."
362..364 Comment "//"
